          "titleEn": "Story & History",
          "grammarMd": "# Newroz\n\n**Newroz** (\"roja nû\" — the new day) is the Kurdish New Year, celebrated on **21 March**, the spring equinox.\n\nThe legend tells of **Kawayê Hesinkar** (Kawa the Blacksmith), who rose against the tyrant **Zuhak** and freed the people. Kawa lit a great **fire (agir)** on the mountains to announce freedom — which is why bonfires, dancing the **govend**, and wearing colourful clothes mark Newroz today.\n\nNewroz is a festival of **spring (bihar)**, renewal, and resistance.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "position": 1,
              "titleKu": "Çîroka Kawa",
              "titleEn": "The Story of Kawa",
